  "statement": "The DNA sequence is composed of a series of nucleotides abbreviated as 'A', 'C', 'G', and 'T'.\nGiven a string S representing a DNA molecule, find all the 10-letter-long sequences (substrings) that occur more than once in the DNA molecule.\n\nPrint the repeated sequences in lexicographical order, each on a new line. If no 10-letter sequence is repeated, print NONE.",
  "inputFormat": "A single string S consisting of characters A, C, G, T.",
  "outputFormat": "Print each repeated 10-letter sequence on a new line, or NONE.",
  "constraints": "1 <= len(S) <= 100000",
  "sampleCases": [
    {
      "input": "AAAAACCCCCAAAAACCCCCCAAAAAGGGTTT",
      "expectedOutput": "AAAAACCCCC\nCCCCCAAAAA",
      "explanation": "Both 10-mers occur more than once."
    },
    {
      "input": "AAAAAAAAAAAAA",
      "expectedOutput": "AAAAAAAAAA",
      "explanation": "Only \"AAAAAAAAAA\" repeats."
    }
  ],
